Id: stor001w
Severity: WARN
Category: filesystem
Check: check_storage
Fix: Add nosuid,nodev to the mount in fstab (or a tmp.mount drop-in) and remount.
References: mount(8), tmpfs(5)
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST CM-6; ISO 8.9; CE Secure configuration

A file system that every user can write to (/tmp, /dev/shm, or /var/tmp
when it is one of its own) is mounted without nosuid or without nodev.
nosuid makes the kernel ignore setuid and setgid bits there, and nodev
makes it refuse to open device files there: without them, a setuid
program or a device node left in a shared directory (through a hard
link, an archive unpacked by root, a compromised service) is honoured.

To fix it, add the options in /etc/fstab, or for a tmpfs that systemd
mounts, in a drop-in for its unit ('systemctl edit tmp.mount',
Options=...); 'mount -o remount' applies them at once.
